<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
<%- include("partials/head", { title: "About - Irish language map", mapPage: false }) %>
</head>

<body>
<%- include("partials/nav", { active: "about" }) %>

    <div class="page">
        <header class="masthead">
            <div class="masthead-text">
                <h1>About</h1>
                <p class="lead">
                    An interactive map of how many people reported being able to
                    speak Irish in each county, across every census from 1851 to
                    2022.
                </p>
            </div>
        </header>

        <div class="prose">
            <p>
                Each county is shaded by the percentage of people aged 3 and over
                who told the census they could speak Irish. The colour scale is
                fixed across every year, so a shade always means the same
                percentage, which lets you watch the long decline and the more
                recent changes. Press <strong>Play animation</strong> on the map
                to step through the census years, or pick a year yourself, and
                click any county to see its exact figure and its trend over time.
            </p>

            <p>
                The map covers all 32 counties: the 26 counties of the Republic
                and the six counties of Northern Ireland. Because the two parts
                of the island ran their censuses differently over time, some
                years are only available for part of the island. The
                <a href="methodology.html">methodology page</a> explains exactly
                what is shown, what is estimated, and how comparable the figures
                are between distant years.
            </p>

            <h2>Credits</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Republic of Ireland figures from the Central Statistics
                    Office (<a href="https://data.cso.ie/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">data.cso.ie</a>).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Northern Ireland figures compiled by
                    <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/phelimbirch.bsky.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Phelim Birch</a>,
                    who generously shared the dataset from his degree project.
                </li>
                <li>
                    County boundaries from Ordnance Survey Ireland (OSi) and
                    Ordnance Survey of Northern Ireland (OSNI).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Map rendering by <a href="https://leafletjs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Leaflet</a>.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                The project is open source. You can read the code, report an
                issue, or download the data on
                <a href="https://github.com/ACoci86/irish-language-map" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>
    </div>

<script src="js/nav.js"></script>

</body>

</html>
